WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:06.530
I've found peace in reminding myself
that their memories live on inside us.

2
00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:11.550
And this is one of the best things
that they leave with us,

3
00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:13.050
is all those memories.

4
00:00:15.190 --> 00:00:21.390
I want to take that one step further
and encourage you, each one of you,

5
00:00:21.530 --> 00:00:25.530
including myself and our growing children:

6
00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:29.790
any memory that we have of him,
let us try to honor and be like him.

7
00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:35.670
Let us try to be good and always open,
whether it's our homes, whether it's our arms.

8
00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:38.830
And obviously many of us, all of us,
are already doing this.

9
00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:41.150
My point is, look for opportunities in life

10
00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:44.890
to honor them in memory
and to honor them in action.

11
00:00:45.990 --> 00:00:48.670
Because at the end of the day,
we have these role models around us

12
00:00:48.670 --> 00:00:50.330
that show us so much good.

13
00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:51.710
Look at our family.

14
00:00:51.750 --> 00:00:53.490
Look at how we're all bonded together like this.

15
00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:57.470
Look at Jonathan taking action on what it means
to be a Gudai, to be a Yeffet,

16
00:00:57.470 --> 00:00:59.450
to be a Norsoph, to be a part of this family.

17
00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:03.370
And so with that, I just encourage each one of us,

18
00:01:03.890 --> 00:01:07.510
even if not in this moment, right,
but through grief and through processing,

19
00:01:07.510 --> 00:01:11.170
to get to that point where we take action
and honor them

20
00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:14.070
by doing a little more than we might have done.
